[center][img]https://i.imgur.com/QaWstlC.png[/img][/center]

ESP Explorer AE is an in-game explorer and utility menu for Fallout 4 Anniversary Edition.

Browse your load order, inspect records, find items, spawn NPCs, add spells or perks, manage inventory, and teleport to cells without leaving the game. It is built for players who want fast access to the data inside their mod list without opening the console or alt-tabbing.

[list]
[*]Search plugins, records, forms, inventory, NPCs, cells, objects, spells, and perks.[/*]
[*]Right-click records for actions that make sense for that record type.[/*]
[*]Favorite useful records and jump back to recently viewed entries.[/*]
[*]Use advanced filters when a large load order needs more than a simple search box.[/*]
[*]View plugin diagnostics, record details, action history, and logs from inside the menu.[/*]
[*]Customize the look with themes, font sizing, language files, and optional Pip-Boy color sync.[/*]
[/list]

[center][img]https://i.imgur.com/QaWstlC.png[/img][/center]

[center][b][img]https://i.imgur.com/KRjnKOf.png[/img][/b][/center]

[list]
[*]In-game plugin browser for ESP, ESM, and ESL files.[/*]
[*]Dedicated tabs for inventory, items, NPCs, cells, objects, spells, and perks.[/*]
[*]Global search across plugins and records.[/*]
[*]Inventory browser with category tabs, equipped filtering, stack details, and quick actions.[/*]
[*]Give, spawn, drop, remove, equip, unequip, duplicate, use, and teleport actions where supported.[/*]
[*]Weapon and armor mod inspection with attach and detach support from the inventory tab.[/*]
[*]Context-aware menus, clipboard copy tools, favorites, and recent records.[/*]
[*]Rule-based filters with saved rules, regex support, hidden plugin management, and global plugin search.[/*]
[*]Action History with best-effort undo for supported actions.[/*]
[*]Optional component substitution so crafting components can be given as usable scrap items.[/*]
[*]Built-in log viewer with copy and export support.[/*]
[*]Data-driven themes and multi-language support.[/*]
[*]Basic controller support with optional gamepad navigation.[/*]
[/list]

[center][size=2]Themes are data-driven. Add or edit .ini theme files in Data/Interface/ESPExplorerAE/themes to customize the menu without rebuilding the plugin.[/size][/center]

[center][size=2]Some shipped translations were created with LLM assistance and may contain mistakes. English is the reference language.[/size][/center]

[center][size=2]Want to make your own translation? Copy en.ini into Data/Interface/ESPExplorerAE/lang, rename it to your language code, translate the values, and optionally add sName, sFontFiles, and sGlyphRanges in the Language section if your language needs custom display text or font coverage.[/size][/center]


[center][img]https://i.imgur.com/QaWstlC.png[/img][/center]

[center][img]https://i.imgur.com/4xgIdrp.png[/img][/center]

[list=1]
[*]Install the requirements: F4SE and Address Library.[/*]
[*]Install this mod with your mod manager, or drop the files into your Fallout 4 game folder.[/*]
[*]Launch the game through F4SE.[/*]
[/list]

The default toggle key is INSERT. You can rebind it at any time. The config file is created automatically next to the plugin in the F4SE\Plugins folder.

[center][img]https://i.imgur.com/QaWstlC.png[/img][/center]

[center][img]https://i.imgur.com/vCq3zR1.png[/img][/center]

[list]
[*]Made for Fallout 4 Anniversary Edition runtime 1.11.191.0.[/*]
[*]Requires F4SE.[/*]
[*]Requires Address Library.[/*]
[*]Supports all plugin types.[/*]
[*]Works with or without the official DLCs.[/*]
[*]Designed to be safe to install or uninstall mid-save.[/*]
[/list]

[center][size=3]This mod may conflict with other in-game explorer, item menu, or input-hook mods. The following mods may work for some setups, but have been reported to cause issues:[/size][/center]

[center][size=3][color=#ff0000]
[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/56922]P71 In Game Shop Mod Explorer[/url]
[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/99301]Fast AddItem Menu[/url][/color][/size]
[/center]

[center][img]https://i.imgur.com/QaWstlC.png[/img][/center]

[center][img]https://i.imgur.com/BbRvQ3C.png[/img][/center]

If something breaks, keep the report short and useful.

[list]
[*]What happened.[/*]
[*]How to reproduce it.[/*]
[*]Your mod list or anything unusual that might matter.[/*]
[*]A screenshot or log if you have one.[/*]
[/list]

Bug reports with clear steps are much easier to fix than reports that only say it does not work.

You can report bugs in two places: 
[list]
[*][url=https://github.com/DeisDev/ESP-Explorer-AE/issues]Github[/url][/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/102223?tab=bugs]Nexus Bug Tracker[/url][/*]
[/list]

